    {
      "id": "ceded",
      "summary": "Bytes the kit shipped and the host has since TAKEN OVER through a signed door (ADR-010). The kit never writes one again -- not to replace it, not to restore it -- and it never vouches for it again either: every reconciliation names it, and where upstream has moved on it says so, because a host that stopped receiving a file must be able to see what it is no longer receiving. `introduced` and `collision` are deliberately unanswered: a path can only be ceded from a row, so neither can be computed, and one that were would be refused rather than defaulted.",
